":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"unknowns":["Requeue consumer, buffer availability and operation identity preservation.","Meaning of full commit provenance and persistence after return."]},{"id":"B7","primary_activity":"A1","execution_owner":"Paxos replica handleCommitShort invocation; dispatcher unread","protocol_context":"Short Commit for an existing local instance","trigger":"CommitShort message","legal_preconditions":["Sender selection and the relationship between short commit and retained commands remain unread."],"implementation_guards":["Returns for a missing instance.","Returns for an already COMMITTED instance.","Returns for a ballot below inst.bal."],"reads":["Existing instance status, ballot and commands"],"writes":["COMMITTED status","inst.bal=commit.Ballot"],"durable_effects":["Records metadata and retained commands conditionally; no explicit sync call in this handler."],"external_effects":[],"important_branches":["Commands and vbal are retained without reassignment.","No command-presence or command-identity check appears in this handler."],"async_boundaries":[],"produces_fact_ids":["F4"],"consumes_fact_ids":[],"cross_activity_effects":{"A5":"Changes local execution eligibility while relying on existing command contents."},"existing_protections":["Existing-instance requirement.","Committed-state and ballot guards."],"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"unknowns":["Which outbound paths use short commits and what prior delivery they establish.","Producer of the retained command representation is not necessarily B3 and is not assigned without reading admission and broadcast paths."]},{"id":"B8","primary_activity":"A5","execution_owner":"Replica.executeCommands loop","protocol_context":"Ordered instance prefix after executedUpTo","trigger":"Loop iteration finding a nonnil instance with nonnil commands and COMMITTED status","legal_preconditions":["Loop startup and shared-state synchronization remain unread."],"implementation_guards":["Visits instances from executedUpTo+1 through crtInstance.","Stops on the first ineligible instance.","Direct value replies require Dreply, leader bookkeeping and client proposals."],"reads":["Shutdown","executedUpTo and crtInstance","Instance commands, status and client proposals","Dreply and State"],"writes":["Application state through Command.Execute","executedUpTo after each eligible instance"],"durable_effects":[],"external_effects":["Direct-reply branch calls Execute and ReplyProposeTS for each command.","Other branch executes only PUT commands."],"important_branches":["Commands without direct client reply bookkeeping are filtered to PUT.","Advancement records loop processing, including commands skipped by that filter."],"async_boundaries":["Application calls and reply helper calls occur before prefix advancement.","The loop shares instance data with protocol handlers.","When no execution occurs it briefly locks/unlocks M and sleeps."],"produces_fact_ids":["F5"],"consumes_fact_ids":["F4"],"cross_activity_effects":{"A7":"Requests successful client replies carrying values returned by application execution."},"existing_protections":["Contiguous-prefix traversal.","Nonnil instance and command checks plus local COMMITTED status."],"source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"unknowns":["Execute semantics and response delivery.","Alignment of command and client-proposal slices.","Persistence and reconstruction of execution progress."]}],"facts":[{"id":"F1","meaning":"The local IsLeader flag has been set true; this assertion does not establish exclusive or quorum-backed authority.","identity":{"replica":"Replica object and r.Id"},"established_by":["B1"],"consumed_by":["B4","B5"],"validity_context":"Current in-memory replica state after initialization or BeTheLeader.","representation":["r.IsLeader"],"invalidators":[],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"In-memory only in supplied code.","recovery":"Constructor receives an initial flag from master registration; restart authority semantics are unread.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:24:163","run.go:23:103"],"unknowns":["Constructor is an additional observed producer not expanded into a Behavior.","Leadership loss and other flag writers are unread.","Additional consumers in run and admission are unread."]},{"id":"F3","meaning":"The matching prepare-reply counter reached its local threshold and the handler assigned client-proposal commands or a NOOP to the instance, set its ballot to lastTriedBallot and marked it ACCEPTED.","identity":{"replica":"r.Id","instance":"preply.Instance","attempt":"lb.lastTriedBallot","commands":"Threshold branch's assigned lb.cmds"},"established_by":["B4"],"consumed_by":[],"validity_context":"Local representation established by the prepare-reply threshold branch. No distinct-participant quorum or selected-value guarantee is inferred.","representation":["lb.prepareOKs","lb.cmds","inst.cmds","inst.bal","inst.status"],"invalidators":["B2","B3","B4","B5","B6","B7"],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"Metadata write and Sync are requested conditionally; command durability is not established.","recovery":"Reconstruction and attempt reset are unread.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"unknowns":["bcastAccept is a called but unread consumer of instance state.","Counter provenance, self contribution and response uniqueness.","Relationship of this assignment to prior accepted values requires surrounding code."]},{"id":"F4","meaning":"The local instance status is COMMITTED. This common assertion does not by itself establish command presence, global agreement, durable retention or application completion.","identity":{"replica":"r.Id","instance":"instanceSpace index"},"established_by":["B5","B6","B7"],"consumed_by":["B2","B8"],"validity_context":"Current local instance after an accept-reply threshold, accepted full Commit, or accepted CommitShort. Command and ballot fields depend on the producing path.","representation":["instanceSpace[index].status == COMMITTED"],"invalidators":["B4"],"reinterpreters":[],"durability":"All three observed producers request metadata writes when Durable; only the accept-reply producer explicitly calls sync.","recovery":"Prepare handling can send retained committed commands; disk reconstruction is unknown.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538","paxos/paxos.go:539:666","paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"unknowns":["B4 has no visible committed-state guard; whether such a later invocation is legal or reachable remains unknown.","Ballot construction and unread admission may introduce additional mutations.","CommitShort does not establish nonnil commands.","Crash invalidation and reconstruction are not mapped."]}],"surfaces":[{"entry_point":"Replica.BeTheLeader","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B1"],"reason":"Local callback mutation is mapped; master caller and authority transition semantics remain deferred.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:24:163"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.handlePrepare and Replica.handleAccept","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B2","B3"],"reason":"Local branch effects are described without equating replies to durable acceptance.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.handlePrepareReply and Replica.handleAcceptReply","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B4","B5"],"reason":"Threshold and ballot branches are mapped; response provenance and legal initialization remain open.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.handleCommit and Replica.handleCommitShort","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B6","B7"],"reason":"Distinct command installation and retention paths are mapped separately; outbound selection remains deferred.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:398:538"],"high_consequence":true},{"entry_point":"Replica.executeCommands and Replica.recover","disposition":"mapped","behavior_ids":["B8","B9","B10"],"reason":"Application processing, request enqueue and recovery entry are separated. The unread dispatch handoff remains explicit.","source_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:667:736"],"high_consequence":true}]},"directed_question":null,"parameters":{},"materials":[{"id":"paxos/paxos.go:539:666","file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":539,"end_line":666,"kind":"code_observation","text":"func (r *Replica) handlePrepareReply(preply *PrepareReply) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance]\n\tlb := r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance].lb\n\n\tif preply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = preply.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.Ballot < lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.Ballot > lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\tlb.nacks++\n\t\tif lb.nacks+1 > r.N>>1 {\n\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(preply.Instance)\n\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(preply.Instance)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif preply.VBallot > lb.ballot {\n\t\tlb.ballot = preply.VBallot\n\t\tlb.cmds = preply.Command\n\t}\n\n\tlb.prepareOKs++\n\tif r.defaultBallot[preply.AcceptorId] < preply.DefaultBallot {\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[preply.AcceptorId] = preply.DefaultBallot\n\t}\n\n\tif lb.prepareOKs < r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize() && len(preply.Command) != 0 {\n\t\tr.totalRecNum += len(preply.Command)\n\t\tr.Println(\"totalRecNum:\", r.totalRecNum)\n\t}\n\n\t// TODO: In the following we update lb.cmds,\n\t// ignoring `lb.cmds = preply.Command` executed\n\t// previously. This is strange\n\n\tif lb.prepareOKs+1 >= r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize() {\n\t\tif lb.clientProposals != nil {\n\t\t\tcmds := make([]state.Command, len(lb.clientProposals))\n\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(lb.clientProposals); i++ {\n\t\t\t\tcmds[i] = lb.clientProposals[i].Command\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tlb.cmds = cmds\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tlb.cmds = state.NOOP()\n\t\t}\n\t\tinst.cmds = lb.cmds\n\t\tinst.bal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.status = ACCEPTED\n\n\t\tm := int32(math.MaxInt32)\n\t\tcount := 0\n\t\tfor _, e := range r.defaultBallot {\n\t\t\tif e != -1 {\n\t\t\t\tcount++\n\t\t\t\tif e < m {\n\t\t\t\t\tm = e\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif count >= r.Replica.ReadQuorumSize()-1 && m > r.smallestDefaultBallot {\n\t\t\tr.smallestDefaultBallot = m\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[preply.Instance])\n\t\tr.sync()\n\t\tr.bcastAccept(preply.Instance)\n\t\tif len(inst.cmds) != 0 {\n\t\t\tr.totalSendNum += len(inst.cmds)\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"totalSendNum:\", r.totalSendNum)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handleAcceptReply(areply *AcceptReply) {\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance]\n\tlb := r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance].lb\n\n\tif areply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = areply.Ballot\n\t}\n\n\tif inst.status >= COMMITTED {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif areply.Ballot < lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tif areply.Ballot > lb.lastTriedBallot {\n\t\tlb.nacks++\n\t\tif lb.nacks+1 >= r.Replica.WriteQuorumSize() {\n\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(areply.Ballot)\n\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(areply.Instance)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tlb.acceptOKs++\n\tif lb.acceptOKs+1 >= r.Replica.WriteQuorumSize() {\n\t\tinst = r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance]\n\t\tinst.status = COMMITTED\n\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.instanceSpace[areply.Instance])\n\t\tr.sync()\n\n\t\tr.bcastCommit(areply.Instance, inst.bal, inst.cmds)\n\t\tif lb.clientProposals != nil && !r.Dreply {\n\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(inst.cmds); i++ {\n\t\t\t\tpropreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n\t\t\t\t\tlb.clientProposals[i].CommandId,\n\t\t\t\t\tstate.NIL(),\n\t\t\t\t\tlb.clientProposals[i].Timestamp}\n\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(propreply, lb.clientProposals[i].Reply, lb.clientProposals[i].Mutex)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb"},{"id":"paxos/paxos.go:261:397","file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":261,"end_line":397,"kind":"code_observation","text":"\t\tfor n < r.defaultBallot[r.Id] || n < r.maxRecvBallot {\n\t\t\tn += int32(r.N)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tlb.lastTriedBallot = n\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastPrepare(instance int32) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Prepare bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\n\targs := &Prepare{r.Id, instance, r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.lastTriedBallot}\n\n\tn := r.N - 1\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.prepareRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t\tif sent >= n {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n}\n\nvar pa Accept\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastAccept(instance int32) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Accept bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\tpa.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpa.Instance = instance\n\tpa.Ballot = r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.lastTriedBallot\n\tpa.Command = r.instanceSpace[instance].lb.cmds\n\targs := &pa\n\n\tn := r.N - 1\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.acceptRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t\tif sent >= n {\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n}\n\nvar pc Commit\nvar pcs CommitShort\n\nfunc (r *Replica) bcastCommit(instance int32, ballot int32, command []state.Command) {\n\tdefer func() {\n\t\tif err := recover(); err != nil {\n\t\t\tr.Println(\"Commit bcast failed:\", err)\n\t\t}\n\t}()\n\tpc.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpc.Instance = instance\n\tpc.Ballot = ballot\n\tpc.Command = command\n\n\tpcs.LeaderId = r.Id\n\tpcs.Instance = instance\n\tpcs.Ballot = ballot\n\tpcs.Count = int32(len(command))\n\targs := &pc\n\n\tsent := 0\n\tfor q := 0; q < r.N-1; q++ {\n\t\tif !r.Alive[r.PreferredPeerOrder[q]] {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tr.SendMsg(r.PreferredPeerOrder[q], r.commitShortRPC, args)\n\t\tsent++\n\t}\n\n}\n\nfunc (r *Replica) handlePropose(propose *defs.GPropose) {\n\tif !r.IsLeader {\n\t\tpreply := &defs.ProposeReplyTS{FALSE, -1, state.NIL(), 0}\n\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(preply, propose.Reply, propose.Mutex)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\n\tbatchSize := len(r.ProposeChan) + 1\n\n\tproposals := make([]*defs.GPropose, batchSize)\n\tcmds := make([]state.Command, batchSize)\n\tproposals[0] = propose\n\tcmds[0] = propose.Command\n\tfor i := 1; i < batchSize; i++ {\n\t\tprop := <-r.ProposeChan\n\t\tproposals[i] = prop\n\t\tcmds[i] = prop.Command\n\t}\n\n\tr.crtInstance++\n\tr.instanceSpace[r.crtInstance] = &Instance{\n\t\tnil,\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id],\n\t\tPREPARING,\n\t\t&LeaderBookkeeping{proposals, 0, 0, 0, r.Id, nil, -1}}\n\tr.makeBallot(r.crtInstance)\n\n\tinst := r.instanceSpace[r.crtInstance]\n\tlb := inst.lb\n\tr.defaultBallot[r.Id] = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\n\tif lb.lastTriedBallot != r.smallestDefaultBallot {\n\t\tr.bcastPrepare(r.crtInstance)\n\t} else {\n\t\tinst.cmds = cmds\n\t\tinst.lb.cmds = cmds\n\t\tinst.bal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.vbal = lb.lastTriedBallot\n\t\tinst.status = ACCEPTED\n\t\tr.bcastAccept(r.crtInstance)\n\t}\n}\n","content_digest":"0386f6cba4a8ae0791dc9acdd3279cb13d9ca657eb1723e286d946cfde9f6edb"}],"required_material_ids":["paxos/paxos.go:261:397","paxos/paxos.go:539:666"],"projection_level":0,"source_rule":"Orientation, provenance IDs and declaration hints are navigation, not source evidence. Only attached exact source supports current implementation judgments.","selected_question":{"disposition":"needs_specific_evidence","preferred_check":"source_review","requests":[{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":261,"end_line":397,"reason":"Inspect proposal initialization and prepare processing to identify attempt context, reported accepted values, and any path that bypasses or constrains prepare-reply value selection."},{"file":"paxos/paxos.go","start_line":539,"end_line":666,"reason":"Inspect prepare-reply collection and its threshold branch, including value selection, attempt validation, bookkeeping, and subsequent accept processing."}],"question":"When the prepare-reply threshold establishes F3 for an instance and attempt, how does the handler choose betwe